Section: fonts
Priority: optional
Description: Hides non-Latin/Cyrillic Noto fonts from font selection dialogs
 Hides Noto font families for scripts other than Latin and Cyrillic
 (Arabic, Hebrew, Thai, CJK, Devanagari, etc.) from font selection
 dialogs. Only Noto Sans, Noto Serif, Noto Sans Display, Noto Serif
 Display, Noto Sans Mono, and Noto Color Emoji remain visible.
 .
 On install the hidden font files are moved out of the fontconfig search
 paths via dpkg-divert. This is what hides them from Flatpak apps too:
 sandboxes mount the host font dirs read-only at /run/host/fonts, so a
 font absent on the host is absent in every sandbox. The owning font
 packages stay installed; the files are moved back on removal.
 .
 A fontconfig reject rule remains installed as a system-wide fallback
 for any Noto font that ends up in a search path without being diverted.
 .
 The fonts-noto-extra package (all non-Latin/Cyrillic weight variants) is
 removed automatically via Conflicts.

